WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:12.109
Ice melts. Wood burns. Both of them are changes,
but they are not the same kind of change.

2
00:00:12.329 --> 00:00:17.530
One of them makes nothing new. The other
makes a substance that was not there before.

3
00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:23.371
Ice is solid water. Its particles
sit in rows, vibrating on the spot.

4
00:00:23.591 --> 00:00:27.492
Warm it up. The particles gain
energy and vibrate harder.

5
00:00:27.712 --> 00:00:31.056
Soon they break out of their
rows and slide past each other.

6
00:00:31.276 --> 00:00:34.201
The ice has melted. It
is liquid water now.

7
00:00:34.421 --> 00:00:39.437
Same water particles all the way
through. Only their arrangement changed.

8
00:00:39.937 --> 00:00:44.116
Now cool the water down. The
particles lose energy and slow.

9
00:00:44.336 --> 00:00:48.655
They lock back into rows. The
water has frozen into ice again.

10
00:00:48.875 --> 00:00:52.590
You can melt and freeze the same
water a thousand times over.

11
00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:56.897
Nothing new is ever made, and
that makes it a physical process.

12
00:00:57.397 --> 00:01:01.809
Now stir sand into water, and
watch carefully what the sand does.

13
00:01:02.029 --> 00:01:06.998
It sinks to the bottom, but it is
still sand. The water is still water.

14
00:01:07.218 --> 00:01:10.237
Nothing new has been made
here. This is a mixture.

15
00:01:10.457 --> 00:01:14.636
You could filter the sand back out
again, so mixing is physical too.

16
00:01:15.136 --> 00:01:19.920
Now pour vinegar onto bicarbonate
of soda. Predict what will happen.

17
00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.412
It fizzes at once. Bubbles of
a gas pour out of the beaker.

18
00:01:24.632 --> 00:01:29.508
That gas did not exist a moment ago.
It is being made in front of you.

19
00:01:29.728 --> 00:01:34.186
The fizz is not just air escaping.
The two substances are reacting.

20
00:01:34.406 --> 00:01:38.911
New substances have been made, and
you cannot get the old ones back.

21
00:01:39.131 --> 00:01:43.496
A change that makes new substances
is called a chemical reaction.

22
00:01:43.996 --> 00:01:49.105
Here is the one test that settles it.
Can you get the same substance back?

23
00:01:49.325 --> 00:01:54.851
Melt a bar of chocolate, then cool it.
It sets, and it is still chocolate.

24
00:01:55.071 --> 00:02:00.040
Dissolve salt in water, then dry the
water off. The salt is left behind.

25
00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:05.276
Burn wood, and you get ash and smoke.
They never turn back into wood.

26
00:02:05.496 --> 00:02:11.022
Bake a cake, and you cannot un-bake
it. New substances were made.

27
00:02:11.522 --> 00:02:15.423
Fizz can spray. Beakers
can smash. Pans burn.

28
00:02:15.643 --> 00:02:21.077
A scientist lists every risk first,
then plans an action for each one.

29
00:02:21.297 --> 00:02:26.684
Goggles on before you pour. Beakers
on a tray, and two hands to carry.

30
00:02:26.904 --> 00:02:30.897
A grown-up does the heat. And
you never, ever taste anything.

31
00:02:31.397 --> 00:02:35.391
Melting and freezing move the
particles. They make nothing new.

32
00:02:35.611 --> 00:02:39.559
Mixing keeps both substances,
so mixing is physical too.

33
00:02:39.779 --> 00:02:44.376
A reaction makes new substances, and
you cannot get the old ones back.

34
00:02:44.596 --> 00:02:47.243
And goggles go on before
you pour anything.
